#: ncdu-clean:1194
msgid ""
"ncdu-clean: delete files found with ncdu, and keep a record of what was "
"removed.\n"
"\n"
"Commands:\n"
"  browse EXPORT   browse like ncdu, mark items, then choose what to do with "
"them\n"
"  rm PATH...      delete (or quarantine) after checks, and journal it (for "
"scripts)\n"
"  log             show the journal of deletions\n"
"  restore [RUN]   list quarantine runs, or put them back where they came "
"from\n"
"  list EXPORT     flat list, biggest first (for scripts, fzf...)\n"
"\n"
"Typical workflow:\n"
"  ncdu -e -o scan.json /var       # 1. scan (-e adds modification dates)\n"
"  ncdu-clean browse scan.json     # 2. Space: mark; x: choose (delete / "
"quarantine / list)\n"
"  ncdu-clean log                  # 3. find out what was deleted\n"
"  ncdu-clean restore              # 4. undo a quarantine, in whole or in "
"part\n"
msgstr ""

#: ncdu-clean:1208
msgid ""
"Default journal: ~/.local/state/ncdu-clean/deleted.jsonl (/var/log/ncdu-"
"clean.jsonl for root), or $NCDU_CLEAN_LOG."
msgstr ""

